      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "From what a friend of mine told me, the VRChat Devs changed the audio system (codec or whatever it is they use to process voices) they used because some players were complaining that voices in the original one were \"too loud\" (...have these people EVER heard of Earmuff mode or just TURNING DOWN THE VOICE VOLUMES?), so they decided to change it to the same audio system SteamVR itself uses. I'm not sure if it's gonna stay or not, but I've also noticed it myself when I was on a couple of days ago for an RP. I hope they at least address the issue in a future dev blog and or update.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
