      "statusChangeID": "693350280d608ac40bf565cb",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks for the feedback! This isn't exactly a bug report - Steam Audio _does_ sound different from our previous spatilizer. So, nothing is broken or bugged, but you are hearing a difference because there is one.\n\nIn short, audio might sound muffled because the system we used before (ONSP) incorrectly boosted several frequencies. Steam Audio is (mostly) flat in comparison. This is an oversimplification of reality, but close enough for a quick feedback response.\n\nWe fully expect people to perceive the difference, especially if you are _very_ used to ONSP. We'll take your feedback into account as we continue to tune Steam Audio for our use case!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "693351805b948aef889ca544",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68",
