      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "6932aff78b5725807b9245a4",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6932283bcd05e17770f64f59",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This isn't exactly correct, so I want to make sure the correct reasons are out there instead of someone reading this and assuming it's true:\n\nWe didn't swap to Steam Audio because some players complained that voices were too loud, we swapped for a variety of reasons. We address it in our [patch note video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_rpJ2F_ax9Q), but in short form, ONSP is old, isn't getting updates, and is hard to work with or improve.\n\nIt isn't accurate to call Steam Audio \"the same audio system SteamVR uses.\" Steam Audio is used by [tons of games](https://steamdb.info/tech/SDK/Steam_Audio/) across both VR and flat surfaces, so it's battle tested.\n\nEither way, please let us know if you run into any bugs -- broken audio, not just \"I think this doesn't sound right\". For the latter, give it some time. Audio is incredibly subjective, and the brain is really good at adapting to sound and audio over time.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
